lor. Sweden also won three events, with Estonia winning two."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The freestyle classes were conducted as single-elimination tournaments, with the silver and bronze medals decided by Bergvall-style second- and third-place tournaments. One innovation in scoring occurred in 1928 with the introduction of “bad points”, or “negative points” for Greco-Roman classes. This would remain the standard method of scoring the Olympic wrestling tournaments through " [:a {:href "/editions/22/sports/WRE"} "1988"] ". In this method, wrestlers accumulate bad points for anything other than a win by fall. The scoring would change slightly over the years but, in 1928, a win by decision cost a wrestler one bad point, while a loss by fall or decision brought three bad points. Once a wrestler had received five or more bad points, he was eliminated from the tournament. In the early rounds, this scoring system was effectively a double-elimination system."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/121669"} "Bantamweight, Greco-Roman (≤58 kg), Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "2 –  4 August 1928"] "\n" [:td {} "19"] "\n" [:td {} "19"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/121710"} "Featherweight, Greco-Roman (≤60 kg), Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "2 –  5 August 1928"] "\n" [:td {} "20"] "\n" [:td {} "20"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/121754"} "Lightweight, Greco-Roman (≤67½ kg), Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "2 –  5 August 1928"] "\n" [:td {} "19"] "\n" [:td {} "19"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/121797"} "Middleweight, Greco-Roman (≤75 kg), Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "2 –  5 August 1928"] "\n" [:td {} "17"] "\n" [:td {